# Line endings, pinned to the repository rather than to the machine.
#
# Why this file exists (v2.9.18, 2026-09-03). `core.autocrlf=true` was checking
# out CRLF while `data/universe.json` sat in the worktree as LF. `git status`
# reported the file clean for weeks — from its stat cache, without ever comparing
# content. The first git operation to touch it rewrote all 3318 line endings
# (281,769 -> 285,087 bytes) with a content diff of exactly zero, which is the
# worst shape a diff can have: a whole-file change that any real edit could hide
# inside.
#
# autocrlf is a per-machine git config and this repository is cloned on more than
# one machine, so the setting drifts. .gitattributes travels with the repository.
#
# Verified before adding: the repository already stores LF (autocrlf=true converts
# on commit), so this pins the worktree without rewriting a single blob and
# without creating a normalisation commit. That matters specifically because
# `data/ab-track/frozen-*.json` must keep exactly one commit — a repo-wide
# renormalisation would have silently voided the gate A integrity check.

* text=auto eol=lf
